   *
   * Five keys. TWO ARE LIVE BELOW; THREE ARE WRITTEN OUT AND COMMENTED, and
   * the split is deliberate rather than unfinished.
   *
   * The two live ones name components that already exist — TrustBand and
   * AreaBand, the same two general-dentistry and the three hubs already use —
   * so registering them costs nothing and breaks nothing.
   *
   * The three commented ones name components that DO NOT EXIST YET. A static
   * import of a missing file fails `astro check` and every build in the
   * repository, including the ones sibling agents are running right now, so
   * the import and the entry land in the SAME commit as the component file,
   * which is also the order Wave A shipped in (components first, registrations
   * second). Each block below is the finished entry: create the named file,
   * add its import beside the three at the top of this file, uncomment the
   * entry, and nothing else changes. The PHP select already carries all five
   * keys — a key registered there and not here renders nothing and warns,
   * which is safe only because no page holds a row for any of them yet
   * (checked against the live endpoint, not assumed).
   *
   * EVERY STRING BELOW IS FROZEN COPY, and on four of the five bands part of
   * it is a live `sections` row today. That is the code_section trade, taken
   * band by band and recorded in the wave's block-map: the row stays movable
   * and removable in wp-admin, the words become a developer edit HERE, and the
   * `sections` rows stay in WordPress but stop feeding the render. Site data
   * is NOT frozen — paragraphs carry `{street}` / `{city}` / `{phone}` /
   * `{phone_href}` tokens where the templates interpolate src/data/contact.ts,
   * and the component substitutes them at render, so an address or a phone
   * change is still one field in Practice Settings.
   */

  /**
